/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2677:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:11417:      "docstring": "Assemble and place enlarged sprites on a canvas using legend-panel instructions.\n\nInput structure:\n- Color-6 separators divide the grid into a left legend column and a main canvas.\n- Each legend panel has (top to bottom): a unit sprite, a frame template, a 5x5 bordered square with a position-marker pixel, and a 3x3 rotation clock-hand.\n\nRule:\n- Tile the unit sprite into each active cell of the frame to build an enlarged composite.\n- Rotate the composite per the clock-hand direction (up=0, right=90, down=180, left=270 degrees).\n- Place it on the canvas anchored at the position encoded by the marker pixel's row/col in the bordered square's 3x3 inner grid.\n\nKey insight: The marker pixel's position in a 3x3 grid jointly encodes vertical and horizontal anchor alignment (start/middle/end).",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2678:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:11581:        "separators",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2679:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:12286:      "docstring": "Recolor a cropped template and repeat it according to a component-count stencil.\n\nInput structure:\n- Solid blue (1) separator rows or columns split the grid into four sections.\n- Section 1 is a black-background shape template; section 2 is a component-count stencil.\n- Sections 3 and 4 are solid color swatches for output foreground and background.\n\nRule:\n- Crop section 1 to the bbox of its non-black pixels and recolor it with the two swatches.\n- Count 4-connected non-black components in section 2.\n- Repeat the recolored crop that many times, inserting one background-colored row/column between copies.\n\nKey insight: The second section encodes only the repeat count; the output orientation\nis inherited from whether the input separators are columns or rows.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2680:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:12291:        "transform": "crop the section-1 template to its non-bg bbox, recolor template pixels with section-3 color and bg pixels with section-4 color, then repeat the crop once per 4-connected component in section 2 with a section-4-colored separator row/col between copies",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2681:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:12292:        "grid_shape": "horizontal or vertical strip determined by separator orientation"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2682:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:12377:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2683:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:12378:        "separators",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2684:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:12708:      "docstring": "Scale a minority cell's inner pattern up to the cell-grid level, completing a fractal overlay.\n\nInput structure:\n- Grid divided into NxN cells by separator lines of a single color.\n- Most cells share an identical interior pattern (majority); a few have a distinct pattern (minority).\n\nRule:\n- Extract the inner pixel pattern from the minority cell.\n- Treat each pixel as a cell-sized stamp: active pixels → minority pattern, inactive → majority pattern.\n- Position this scaled-up pattern on the cell grid so existing minority cells align with active pixels.\n- Fill in all remaining active positions with the minority pattern.\n\nKey insight: The minority cell's interior is a miniature blueprint of where minority cells should appear at the grid scale — fractal self-similarity.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2685:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:12734:        "catalog:separator_line",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2686:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:12844:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2687:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14211:      "docstring": "Look up query glyphs in a reference table and mark whether they form a line.\n\nInput structure:\n- Teal background with two full-width pink separator rows.\n- Above the first separator is a query row of 5x5 glyph cells.\n- Between separators is a reference table of the same 5x5 cells; a glyph is\n  identified by both its color and its 3x3 shape.\n\nRule:\n- Green-fill the background inside every table cell whose glyph exactly\n  appears in the query row.\n- If the matched table cells form one complete row or one complete column,\n  also green-fill the query band and the bottom verdict band.\n- Otherwise leave the query band unchanged and fill the bottom verdict band red.\n\nKey insight: The bottom color is not a count; it is the yes/no answer to\nwhether the queried glyphs align as a full row or column in the table.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2688:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14215:        "src": "query glyph cells s above the first separator row",
