/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2692:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17805:        "grid_shape": "one row of panels, same panel size as input, with one bg separator column between panels"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2693:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17892:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2694:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19421:      "docstring": "Replace each marker below the separator with the mapped top legend square centered on that marker.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background surrounds a top legend, one solid non-background separator row, and a lower marker field.\n- The legend contains equal-size filled square sprites, with a singleton marker below each sprite and aligned to its center column.\n- The lower field contains only background and marker colors from the legend.\n\nRule:\n- Pair legend markers to legend sprites by left-to-right position.\n- Discard the legend and separator; keep the grid width and the rows below the separator.\n- In the lower field, replace every marker pixel by a filled square of the paired sprite color, centered at the marker location.\n\nKey insight: The top area is a positional color legend, and the actual output is the post-separator marker field expanded by that legend.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2695:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19429:        "grid_shape": "rows below the separator, same width"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2696:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19514:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2697:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19938:      "docstring": "Fold each straight red rod at its black marker, leaving the gray-anchored side fixed.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Each foreground object is a straight horizontal or vertical 4-connected rod.\n- Each rod contains many pixels of one line color, one endpoint marker, and one\n  interior control marker.\n\nRule:\n- For every rod, keep the segment from the endpoint marker through the control\n  marker unchanged.\n- Move the line-color tail on the far side of the control marker to a\n  perpendicular ray starting next to that marker.\n- Choose the perpendicular direction with more space to the grid edge.\n\nKey insight:\n- The endpoint marker identifies the fixed side of the rod, while the control\n  marker is the hinge; the tail folds into the larger open half-plane.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2698:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19989:        "fold",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2699:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19990:        "folds",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2700:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:22022:      "docstring": "Fill every row from the nearest marked horizontal bar, turning bar rows and color-boundary ties into separator rows.\n\nInput structure\n- A dominant background fills the grid except for full-width horizontal bars and one vertical marker column.\n- Outside the marker column, every row is monochrome: either background or a source bar color.\n- Background rows share one marker color in the marker column; source bar rows share the other.\n\nRule\n- Each non-source row takes the color of the nearest source bar, with that row's marker-column pixel set to the source-marker color.\n- If a row is exactly midway between nearest bars of different colors, make the whole row the source-marker color.\n- Each original source bar row becomes a source-marker row with the marker-column pixel changed to the background-row marker color.\n\nKey insight\n- The marked bars are horizontal seeds for a one-dimensional nearest-seed partition over rows; equal-distance rows are separators only when the competing seed colors differ.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2701:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:22027:        "transform": "recolor each row by the nearest source bar color; each source bar row becomes a marker separator row, and equal-distance rows between different bar colors become plain separator rows"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2702:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:22112:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2703:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:22113:        "separators",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2704:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:22150:        "grid_shape": "5x17 input with separator columns -> 5x5 output"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2705:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:22246:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2706:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23449:      "docstring": "Infer the background, rotate the whole input 90 degrees counterclockwise, and stack two framed copies vertically.\n\nInput structure:\n- Blue is absent from the input.\n- One rare marker color appears in exactly two pixels.\n- The background is the unique non-marker color whose removal leaves exactly two 4-connected foreground objects, each with one marker pixel and one body color.\n- The whole grid, including background and foreground objects, is the sprite to transform.\n\nRule:\n- Rotate the entire input grid 90 degrees counterclockwise.\n- Create a blue one-pixel frame around two vertical copies of the rotated grid.\n- Use the input background color for the two endpoints of every horizontal frame/separator row.\n\nKey insight: The output is not a crop of the foreground objects; it is two copies of the complete rotated input, separated and enclosed by a newly added blue border.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2707:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23456:        "grid_shape": "rotated input width plus side borders by two rotated input heights plus three frame/separator rows"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2708:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23558:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2709:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23974:      "docstring": "Extract the compact table of solid cells hidden inside a separator lattice.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has full-width and full-height bars of one separator color, dividing it into rectangular cells.\n- Most cells contain a repeating multicolor pattern, while a contiguous rectangle of cells is solid monochrome.\n\nRule\n- Split the input into lattice cells using the full separator rows and columns.\n- Keep the cells whose full interior is one color, crop to their occupied rectangle, and output those colors.\n\nKey insight\n- The periodic pattern is noise; only completely solid lattice cells encode the reduced output grid.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2710:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23978:        "src": "solid monochrome cells inside a full-row/full-column separator lattice over a periodic pattern",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2711:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23980:        "transform": "split at separator bars; identify cells whose interior is a single color; crop to the occupied solid-cell rectangle and replace each cell by its color",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2712:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:24068:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2713:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25561:      "docstring": "Reflect the solid rectangular source objects across the full separator line and color the gap with the separator color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background contains one full-width or full-height one-pixel\n  separator line in a non-background color.\n- One other foreground color forms solid rectangular objects, all strictly on the same side of that separator.\n- Remaining non-background pixels are scattered distractors.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the input grid shape and unchanged pixels outside each affected corridor.\n- Mirror each source object across the separator line.\n- For every source object, recolor the rectangular strip between the\n  original object and its reflection to the separator color, then paint the\n  reflected object in the source color.\n\nKey insight:\n- The full straight line is a mirror axis; the real objects are identified\n  structurally as the only solid rectangles confined to one side, while\n  scattered pixels are noise that may be overwritten inside the corridor.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2714:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25565:        "src": "solid rectangular foreground objects all on one side of the full separator row/column",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2715:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25566:        "dst": "their mirror positions across the separator line",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2716:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25567:        "transform": "copy each source object by reflection; recolor the rectangular strip between each source object and its mirror to the separator color, overwriting background or distractor pixels inside that strip"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2717:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25573:        "catalog:separator_line",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2718:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25666:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2719:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26318:      "docstring": "Extract the single plain rectangle and redraw it with the aligned rectangles' border-relative marker pattern.\n\nInput structure:\n- The boundary color is the background/separator.\n- Foreground objects are dense rectangular regions; exactly one rectangle has only its base color.\n- Other rectangles contain their base color plus marker pixels.\n\nRule:\n- Crop the only plain rectangle; this crop is the output canvas.\n- Use marked rectangles whose row span overlaps the plain rectangle's row span.\n- Transfer their marker pixels by preserving each marker run's distance from the nearest rectangle edges.\n\nKey insight:\n- The marked rectangles are examples of an edge-relative pattern, so the missing plain rectangle receives the same pattern resized to its own dimensions.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2720:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26429:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2721:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26577:      "docstring": "Within each horizontal pair of two-color panels, swap the motif masks and recolor each pasted mask with the source panel's base color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A separator color forms full blank rows and at least one full blank column.\n- The non-separator area is split into row bands, each containing exactly two same-shaped rectangular panels.\n- Each panel has a dominant base color and one minority motif color.\n\nRule:\n- For every row band, clear each panel to its own base color.\n- Paste the right panel's motif mask into the left panel using the right base color.\n- Paste the left panel's motif mask into the right panel using the left base color.\n\nKey insight:\n- The motif colors themselves are distractors; only each motif's shape mask and the two panel base colors are exchanged.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2722:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26583:        "match_cond": "s.panel and d are paired across the separator columns within the same row band",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2723:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26669:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2724:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27288:      "docstring": "Combine the left, middle, and right ordered objects from three separated panels.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid is three HxH panels separated by one-cell vertical separator bars.\n- The background is the dominant color, and each panel contains exactly three same-color 4-connected foreground objects.\n\nRule\n- Build a new HxH background canvas.\n- From the left panel copy its leftmost object, from the middle panel copy its middle object, and from the right panel copy its rightmost object.\n\nKey insight\n- The separator bars create three aligned layers, and the panel's own left-to-right object order selects which object survives in the merged output.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2725:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27294:        "transform": "copy object 1 from panel 1, object 2 from panel 2, and object 3 from panel 3; discard the other objects and separator columns",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2726:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27295:        "grid_shape": "3 HxH panels with two separator columns -> HxH output"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2727:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27377:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2728:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27515:      "docstring": "Build a color-labeled shape-equivalence table from the objects listed on the right edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background contains one main 4-connected object for each foreground color.\n- The rightmost column has one singleton pixel of each foreground color, listed top-to-bottom.\n- Those singleton pixels define the row and column order of the output table.\n\nRule:\n- Normalize each main object to its tight mask and compare masks up to rotation or reflection.\n- Draw 2x2 color labels across the top and down the left, separated by one background row/column.\n- For each off-diagonal table cell, paint a 2x2 red block when the two labeled objects have the same shape under rotation/reflection, otherwise paint a 2x2 grey block.\n- Leave diagonal cells and all separators as background.\n\nKey insight:\n- Object positions and original orientations are distractors; the relation is dihedral shape equivalence, while the right-edge legend fixes the table order.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2729:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27521:        "transform": "normalize each object's mask; red-fill off-diagonal table cells for object pairs with the same shape under rotation/flip, grey-fill all other off-diagonal cells; diagonal cells and separators remain background",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2730:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27638:        "separators",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2731:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27674:      "docstring": "Decode a block-grid image by swapping each sprite-coded cell with a solid cell and each blank cell with the sprite.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid is partitioned by black separator rows and columns into equal-size\nsquare blocks. Each block is either a copy of one two-color sprite or a\nuniform blank block of the sprite's minority color; grey pixels are erased\ncells that act as wildcards.\n\nRule\nInfer the repeated sprite from fully visible mixed-color blocks. Replace a\nblock matching that sprite, ignoring grey erasures, with a solid block of\nthe sprite's majority color. Replace a uniform blank block with the sprite.\nSeparator rows and columns, including grey erasures on them, become black.\n\nKey insight\nThe small sprite is a block-level code for one macro-cell state, and the\nuniform minority-color block is the other state; the output renders the\nopposite code in each macro-cell while cleaning erased pixels.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2732:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27680:        "transform": "infer the sprite from fully visible mixed-color blocks; sprite-coded blocks become solid majority-color blocks, blank blocks become the sprite, and separator/erasure pixels become black"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2733:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27766:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2734:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29803:      "docstring": "Move each source pixel toward the separator when it matches its aligned reference pixel, otherwise to the far edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- A single full separator line is part of a rectangular frame; the frame's\n  extra cells mark the reference side.\n- On the reference side, one row or column of colored pixels is aligned\n  with one row or column of source pixels on the opposite side.\n- Each side has its own dominant background color.\n\nRule:\n- Compare each source pixel with the reference pixel on the same row or column.\n- If their colors match, place the source pixel in the cell adjacent to the\n  separator on the source side.\n- If their colors differ, place the source pixel on the far outer edge along\n  the same row or column.\n- Erase the original source pixels to the source-side background; keep the\n  frame and reference pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\nThe extra frame cells identify which side is the reference; equality with the\naligned reference pixel decides whether each source pixel moves inward or outward.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2735:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29807:        "src": "single source pixels on the open side of the separator, aligned with reference pixels on the framed side",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2736:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29808:        "path": "straight line perpendicular to the separator, staying on the same row or column",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2737:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29809:        "dst": "adjacent to the separator when the source color equals the aligned reference color; otherwise the far outer edge on the source side",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2738:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29811:        "transform": "erase original source pixels to the source-side background; keep the separator frame and reference pixels unchanged"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2739:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29816:        "catalog:separator_line",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2740:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29905:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2741:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30325:      "docstring": "Draw a blue folded corner-to-corner route through the lone marker's column.\n\nInput structure:\n- A rectangular grid filled with one background color.\n- Exactly one non-background marker pixel; blue is absent from the input.\n\nRule:\n- Preserve the marker and repaint background pixels in its column blue from top to bottom.\n- If the marker is in the unique center column, connect that column to the top-right and bottom-left corners.\n- Otherwise, connect the column to the top-left and bottom-right corners.\n\nKey insight:\nThe marker's column is the route spine; its central vs off-center placement selects which opposite corner pair gets the horizontal edge segments.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2742:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30371:        "folded",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2743:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30710:      "docstring": "Swap the upper two-pixel segment and the lower two-pixel segment around the fixed center pixel.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid is a 5x1 vertical column of individual colored pixels.\n- The middle pixel is a separator between two same-size two-pixel segments.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the middle pixel in place.\n- Reverse the order of the two pixels above the middle.\n- Reverse the order of the two pixels below the middle.\n\nKey insight:\n- The transformation is local vertical order reversal on each side of the center, not a color-specific rule.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2744:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30714:        "src": "5x1 vertical column with a center separator pixel",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2745:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30766:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2746:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31323:      "docstring": "Stagger the two horizontal input regions onto a larger maroon separator canvas.\n\nInput structure:\n- The input is a rectangular grid with an even number of rows.\n- The top half and bottom half are the two regions to preserve.\n- Maroon is absent from the input and is used only as the new separator color.\n\nRule:\n- Create an output with one extra row and one extra column, filled with maroon.\n- Copy the top half into the upper-left corner.\n- Copy the bottom half one row below the top region and one column to the right.\n\nKey insight:\nThe output is not a recoloring of either region; it inserts an L-shaped maroon\ngap by diagonally offsetting the lower half from the upper half.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2747:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31415:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2748:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:34253:      "docstring": "Compress the noisy four-region board split by a solid cross into a 3x3 color map.\n\nInput structure:\n- A single full row and a single full column have the same solid separator color.\n- The separator cross divides the input into four nonempty rectangular regions.\n- Each region has a unique dominant color, with other colors acting as noise.\n\nRule:\n- Find the unique solid same-color row/column pair.\n- Fill the middle row and middle column of the 3x3 output with the separator color.\n- Put the unique dominant color of each quadrant into the corresponding corner.\n\nKey insight:\n- The input grid is a noisy enlarged version of the desired 3x3 layout; the cross marks the coarse cell boundaries.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2749:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:34335:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2750:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:35581:      "docstring": "Compress the stacked colored bars into a compact ordered table with the control pixel on the selected row.\n\nInput structure\n- A background grid contains several full-width colored bars from top to\n  bottom; the last bar is the base/separator color.\n- Each non-base bar may have an aligned three-column comb motif below it,\n  alternating side-pair rows with solid rows.\n- A singleton control pixel sits away from the colored motifs.\n\nRule\n- Make one output row per non-base bar, preserving top-to-bottom order.\n- In that row, paint the bar color once for each solid three-pixel row in\n  its motif, then paint the base-bar color in the separator column.\n- The singleton control pixel sits immediately above the base bar. Among\n  motifs whose open side-pair parity is compatible with that bottom row,\n  put the control pixel in the output row with the fewest solid rows; use\n  horizontal distance to the motif center only to break count ties.\n\nKey insight\n- The vertical comb height is a count, while the control pixel is read by\n  projecting it onto the center gap of compatible comb rows rather than by\n  its vertical band alone.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2751:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:35585:        "src": "full-width colored bars with aligned three-column comb motifs; the final full-width bar is the separator color",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2752:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:35587:        "transform": "paint each row with the bar color repeated once per solid motif row, append the separator color column, and place the singleton control pixel on the row whose open motif center is nearest to it",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2753:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:35589:        "grid_shape": "one row per non-separator bar; columns are count slots plus separator and control-pixel columns"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2754:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:35707:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2755:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:35879:      "docstring": "Add the two missing colored arms of a centered diamond-sprite motif, or clear a completed motif to a blank square.\n\nInput structure\nAn 11x11 board has orange background and pink separator bars forming nine 3x3 cells. Occupied cells contain a four-pixel diamond sprite; the center cell and one neighboring cell are red, and a completed board may also contain one grey and one teal sprite.\n\nRule\nWith only the two red sprites present, preserve the board and add grey and teal diamond sprites 135 degrees clockwise and counterclockwise from the non-center red arm. If those expected grey and teal sprites are already present, output an all-background square whose side length is the total number of sprite pixels.\n\nKey insight\nThe non-center red sprite is an eight-neighbor direction from the center; the other two colored arms are fixed rotations of that direction.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2756:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:35987:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2757:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:37717:      "docstring": "Render the filled-square object counts as compact nested stacks ordered by count rank.\n\nInput structure\nA large noisy grid has a dominant background, scattered non-square noise, and\nfilled monochrome square objects. Each square side length has exactly one\nobject color, and side lengths form consecutive sizes.\n\nRule\nIgnore non-square components. If the lowest square in the scene is of the\nsmallest side length, treat that one smallest square as a distractor and do\nnot count it. For count rank k from left to right, create one block from all\nsquare sizes with at least k remaining objects; draw larger squares first and\nsmaller squares over their upper-left corner, then append one background\nseparator column.\n\nKey insight\nThe output is a count histogram of square side lengths, but each histogram\nslot is rendered as nested upper-left square masks using the side colors.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2758:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:37724:        "transform": "draw each slot as nested upper-left square masks, larger sides first; append one bg separator column after every slot",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2759:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:37725:        "grid_shape": "height is largest side + 1; width is sum of slot widths plus one separator per slot"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2760:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:37831:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2761:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:38240:      "docstring": "Extract the hidden two-color image by compacting the rows and columns of its complete mask.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid contains one pair of colors whose pixels occupy every cell in the\ncross product of their active rows and active columns; all other colors form\nthe surrounding filler or separators.\nRule\nFind that unique color pair, keep exactly the rows and columns touched by\nthe pair, and return the induced subgrid.\nKey insight\nThe target image is not chosen by color id; it is the only two-color mask\nwhose occupied pixels form a full rectangular row/column product after\ndeleting unused rows and columns.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2762:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:38320:        "separators",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2763:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:39568:        "transform": "paint only the matched background gaps; preserve existing foreground pixels and background separator columns"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2764:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:39662:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2765:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:39941:      "docstring": "Expand the second mask into a block grid by stamping the first mask with the two payload colors.\n\nInput structure\n- A background grid has four panels separated by three full-height separator columns.\n- The first two panels contain same-size binary masks; the last two contain solid same-size color squares.\nRule\n- Use the second mask as an outer layout. For each foreground cell in that outer mask, place a tile equal to the first mask, coloring its foreground with the first solid-square color and its background with the second solid-square color; outer background cells become all second solid-square color.\nKey insight\n- The output is the Kronecker product of the two binary masks, with the two right-hand panel colors providing the palette.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2766:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:39945:        "src": "four separator-delimited sections: inner mask, outer mask, and two solid color swatches",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2767:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:40036:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2768:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:40221:      "docstring": "Move each mirrored bottom source pixel to the far end of its trail and redraw the top half as its reflection.\n\nInput structure\n- A solid non-background row separates equal-height top and bottom halves.\n- The top half has one marker color on the background.\n- In the bottom half, exactly one color has positions that mirror the top markers across the separator, and the other color forms trails touching those source pixels.\n\nRule\n- Identify the bottom source color by reflecting each bottom color into the top half and matching the top marker set.\n- For every bottom source pixel, follow its unique 4-connected trail of the other bottom color to the trail endpoint.\n- Clear the old top markers, bottom sources, and trails; place the source color at each endpoint and place the top marker color at the reflected endpoint.\n\nKey insight\n- The top half is only a mirror display of the bottom moving sources; the actual motion is encoded by the trail attached to each bottom source pixel.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2769:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:40225:        "src": "bottom-half source pixels s, identified as the color whose positions reflect to the top marker mask across the separator row",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2770:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:40228:        "transform": "redraw the top marker color at the reflection of each moved source endpoint; keep the separator and background unchanged"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2771:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:40320:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2772:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:40993:        "grid_shape": "height 10; width is the sum of max(h,w) over source rectangles plus one separator column between consecutive rectangles"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2773:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:41083:        "separator",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2774:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:42067:      "docstring": "Move the lower sprite and its pink guide into the upper panel, aligning the sprite to the guide's lower-left branch.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has one dominant background color and one full-width separator row.\n- Below the separator are exactly two foreground roles: a five-pixel guide marker and one monochrome sprite.\n- The guide marker has normalized shape {(0,2), (1,2), (2,0), (2,2), (3,1)} and starts immediately below the separator.\n\nRule\n- Clear the canvas to the background, preserving the separator row.\n- Translate the guide marker upward so its top row becomes row 0.\n- Move the sprite, preserving its color and shape, so the sprite bbox bottom-right aligns to the translated guide's lower-left branch.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker supplies the destination anchor: its lower-left branch cell is where the moved sprite's bbox bottom-right must land.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/1/043/codegen_7.skill.log:2775:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:42071:        "src": "monochrome sprite s below the separator",
