/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2865:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:291:        "dst": "a single polyline in the left canvas starting at the shifted gray marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2866:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:303:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2867:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:367:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2868:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:420:      "docstring": "Fill partitioned regions with concentric colored bands derived from marker pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- Grid partitioned into regions by wall-colored lines.\n- Each region has a dominant base color and a few isolated marker pixels of other colors at varying depths from the region boundary.\n\nRule:\n- For each region, read marker colors ordered by their Chebyshev distance from the boundary to build a color palette.\n- If no marker sits on the boundary itself, the base color leads the palette.\n- Paint every cell with palette[distance mod palette_length], producing repeating concentric rectangular frames that radiate inward.\n\nKey insight: Each marker's depth from the boundary defines its position in the cyclic palette; the pattern then tiles inward automatically.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2869:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:444:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2870:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:453:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2871:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:522:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2872:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:610:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2873:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:875:      "docstring": "Fill periodic progressions that shoot from a unique grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.  Sparse non-bg dots of several colors.\n- All repeating colors originate from the same grid edge (top, bottom,\n  left, or right — the one with the most non-bg dots).\n- Each repeating color has exactly 2 dots per shooting-direction line;\n  their gap defines the step.\n- Every non-bg dot lies on a shooting-direction line that contains a\n  repeating color.\n\nRule:\n- Determine the unique shooting edge; left/right → rows, top/bottom → columns.\n- For each shooting-direction line, the repeating color has exactly 2 dots;\n  step = gap between them, offset = first position mod step.\n- A different-colored dot aligned to the same beat (pos % step == offset) is\n  a companion: it absorbs the ray and becomes the fill color, limiting the\n  fill range to the span between repeating and companion dots.\n- An unaligned dot is a bystander and left untouched.\n- Without a companion the repeating color fills the entire line.\n\nKey insight: the shooting edge is identified by counting boundary dots;\nthe gap between the two marker dots is the period; a companion sharing the\nmodular class acts as a wall that stops the ray and dictates the paint color.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2874:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:883:        "transform": "fill background/marker cells on that path with the trajectory color; ties apply both row and column rules"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2875:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:893:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2876:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:976:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2877:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1158:      "docstring": "Simulate particles along a path with alternating turn direction at collisions.\n\nInput structure:\n- Top-left: 2x2 monochrome blocks define a repeating color cycle (left-to-right).\n- Isolated single pixels of a cycle color: start markers adjacent to the path.\n- A 2x2 monochrome block of a distinct color: end marker.\n\nRule:\n- Each start marker launches a particle moving straight, painting cycle colors in order.\n- On hitting a boundary, paint that cell with the end color and turn 90°.\n- Turn direction alternates: odd collisions → left (CCW), even → right (CW).\n- If the scheduled turn is blocked, the particle stops.\n\nKey insight: The alternating left/right turn rule is the core mechanism; without it the path would be trivial.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2878:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1162:        "src": "start markers: isolated single pixels whose colors belong to a template cycle shown as 2x2 monochrome blocks in the top-left",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2879:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1166:        "transform": "erase the template 2x2 blocks and the 2x2 end block; while moving, recolor visited path cells by the cycle; on collision into template background, paint that collided cell with the end-block color as a corner marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2880:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1168:        "notes": "initial direction is the first adjacent path neighbor in priority R,D,L,U; cycle index starts at the marker’s own color within the cycle; apply independently for each marker"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2881:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1183:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2882:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1269:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2883:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1270:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2884:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1657:      "docstring": "Repaint regions from T-shaped control markers, erase the markers, and optionally rotate based on a color-9 L-marker.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid is a mosaic of monochrome regions.\n- Color 1 forms T-shaped control markers on region boundaries.\n- Some controls use three singleton color-1 pixels around a colored center; that center is a literal replacement color.\n- An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker triggers 90-degree rotation of the output.\n\nRule:\n- For a color-1 T marker, the single stem points at the destination region to repaint.\n- The two diagonal cells behind the stem identify the source region; the destination gets that source region's original color.\n- For a colored-center T marker, the same stem identifies the destination, but the center color is the replacement.\n- All marker cells are filled with the final color of the source-side region.\n- A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: ┐ (corner top-right) → CCW 90°, ┌ (corner top-left) → CW 90°.\n\nKey insight:\n- The stem chooses what changes, while the two diagonals behind the stem choose where the marker itself belongs.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2885:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1661:        "src": "monochrome regions with T-shaped color-1 control markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2886:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1662:        "transform": "recolor the region pointed to by each T stem using the original color from the two diagonal source cells behind the stem; colored-center T markers use the center color instead; erase marker cells into the source-side region",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2887:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1679:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2888:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1744:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2889:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1745:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2890:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1960:      "docstring": "Move colored sprites from the left strip into a framed area at marker-defined targets.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.\n\nRule:\n- For each color, target rows/cols are where both opposite frame edges share that color. Targets are the Cartesian product.\n- Erase each sprite from the left and stamp it centered at every target. Higher sprites cover lower ones.\n\nKey insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2891:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:1979:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2892:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:2032:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2893:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:2033:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2894:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:2193:      "docstring": "Move bordered containers toward same-colored destination markers, charging gray cells to orange.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = 6 (magenta). Black-bordered (0) rectangles with gray (5) / orange (7) interiors.\n- A head sprite (9) sits adjacent to one container edge; a matching destination sprite lies along the movement axis.\n\nRule:\n- Each container translates toward its destination along the head-to-dest axis.\n- Steps = min(head-to-dest distance, number of gray interior cells).\n- Gray cells become orange from the head-facing side inward, one per step.\n\nKey insight: Gray cell count caps movement — a container stops short if it runs out of gray cells to charge.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2895:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:2215:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2896:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:2277:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2897:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:3294:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2898:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:4454:      "docstring": "Assemble scattered rectangular pieces into a rectangle at an L-marker corner.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Non-bg rectangular pieces scattered on the grid.\n- 3-pixel L-marker (2x2 minus one cell) tags the corner; the gap is the corner cell.\n\nRule:\n- rect_col = most common color across all piece pixels; all outer rectangle edges must be rect_col.\n- Translate pieces (no rotation) to tile the rectangle; touching edges must match, with rect_col as wildcard.\n\nKey insight: rect_col acts as wildcard during edge matching — only non-rect_col pixels at shared boundaries must agree.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2899:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:4459:        "dst": "fit against the matching edge d of a jigsaw growing from a corner square tagged by a marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2900:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:4477:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2901:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:4530:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2902:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:4861:      "docstring": "Fit a grey bar into a grey frame by aligning projections with colored columns, then stack colors above.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg, a grey structural color forming two components: a large rectangular frame (slot) and a smaller bar with upward projections.\n- Colored pixels inside the slot mark target columns.\n\nRule:\n- Move the bar upward into the slot so its bottom edge sits one cell above the slot's interior bottom.\n- Shift it horizontally so the bar's upward projections align column-wise with the colored pixels in the slot.\n- Stack the colored pixels immediately above the bar projections in each column.\n\nKey insight: The bar's projections act as keys that must align with the colored-column \"locks\" in the slot.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2903:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:4864:        "summary": "Grey horizontal bars with upward projections move upward into semi-open grey slots, aligning projections with slot openings, then colored pixels within slots move upward to align vertically with the bar's projections",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2904:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:4866:        "src": "grey horizontal bar with upward vertical projections s",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2905:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:4867:        "dst": "semi-open grey slot region with downward colored vertical projections d",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2906:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:4868:        "match_cond": "s.projections align vertically with d.colored_projections (column positions match)",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2907:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:4873:        "multi_step": "Step 1: Identify grey bar s with upward projections and grey slot d with colored downward projections; Step 2: Move s upward into d such that s.projections fit into d.openings with projection-to-projection vertical alignment; Step 3: Move colored pixels upward so they align with bar projections, with bar bottom 1 cell above slot bottom",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2908:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:4875:          "projection-slot alignment",
