/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2932:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5660:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2933:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5661:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2934:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5747:      "docstring": "Slide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color \"marker\" pixel.\n- Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.\n\nRule:\n- Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.\n- Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.\n- Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.\n\nKey insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2935:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5751:        "src": "multi-color sprite s with a unique marker color (minority color inside s)",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2936:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5752:        "dst": "align to isolated border pixel d (same marker color)",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2937:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5753:        "match_cond": "s.marker.color == d.color",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2938:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5754:        "transform": "translate s: if d on top/bottom edge → align col(s.marker) to col(d); else → align row(s.marker) to row(d); clip out-of-bounds pixels"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2939:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5758:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2940:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5768:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2941:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:5814:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2942:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:6119:      "docstring": "Build a red ray network by activating blue blobs via directional green ports.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Large blue blobs with adjacent green pixels marking port directions.\n- Start marker: yellow pixel atop a short red segment at grid bottom.\n\nRule:\n- Extend a ray upward from start; on hitting a blue blob, recolor it red.\n- Activated blobs emit thick rays through green ports until boundary or another blob.\n- Cascade until no new blobs are reached.\n\nKey insight: Green pixels encode ray direction and width; the network activates as a chain reaction from one start point.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2943:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:6141:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2944:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:6199:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2945:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:6522:      "docstring": "Copy colored control-ray ports from one rectangular sprite orientation to every matching transformed sprite.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg is the most common color.\n- Several dense 2-by-N or N-by-2 rectangular sprites are dihedral transforms of one template.\n- Isolated single-pixel control markers sit on rays projected outward from the dominant long edge of some sprites.\n\nRule:\n- For each sprite, the active edge is the long side whose cells have the strongest same-color majority.\n- A control marker seen first along an outward ray from an active-edge cell assigns its color to that template cell.\n- On every transformed sprite, draw that assigned color outward from the corresponding active-edge cell through bg cells until blocked or out of bounds.\n\nKey insight:\n- The marker positions are not absolute; they label cells of a shared rectangular template, then the labels follow each sprite's rotation/reflection.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2946:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:6526:        "src": "single-pixel control markers labeling active-edge cells of rectangular sprites",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2947:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:6530:        "transform": "copy marker labels by dihedral template position across all matching rectangular sprites"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2948:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:6544:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2949:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:6607:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2950:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:6608:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2951:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:6675:      "docstring": "Decode a stamp map: read templates, markers, and palette from a tiled grid, then render stamps.\n\nInput structure:\n- Grid divided into K tile columns (each N wide) separated by 1-col dashed separators.\n- Top band (rows 0..N-1): K template masks, one per tile column.\n- Middle band (rows N+1..2N): marker pixels whose color picks a template.\n- Bottom band (rows 2N+2..): K palette swatches giving the output color per template.\n- Separator rows at rows N and 2N+1 (dashed pattern of sep color).\n\nRule:\n- Each marker's local position (lr, lc) within its tile column determines which N×N output block to stamp.\n- The marker's color identifies which template to use; the palette recolors the template.\n\nKey insight: Marker color encodes template index; local position within tile column encodes stamp block.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2952:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:6679:        "src": "template-color marker pixels s in the middle band (between top templates and bottom palette)",
