/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2973:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:8064:      "docstring": "Assemble colored rectangular sprites into a single tiled rectangle, anchored by a marker pixel.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Several solid-colored rectangular sprites scattered on the grid.\n- One sprite has a unique single-pixel marker (different color) at one corner — this is the anchor.\n\nRule:\n- Identify the anchor sprite (contains the marker pixel) and the remaining pieces.\n- Rotate the anchor so the marker pixel lands at position (0,0) of the output.\n- Pack all remaining pieces (allowing 90° rotations) to tile a complete rectangle with no gaps.\n\nKey insight: The lone marker pixel picks the anchor and fixes the output orientation — it must sit at the top-left corner.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2974:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:8069:        "src": "colored rectangular sprites without grey corner marker s",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2975:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:8097:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2976:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:8164:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2977:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:8598:      "docstring": "Mirror colored sprites using red (2) markers as reflection axes.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Red (2) = marker color.\n- Colored sprites appear near red markers.\n\nRule:\n- Red line within a sprite (vertical or horizontal) → mirror payload across that axis.\n- Single red pixel in a mixed sprite → point-reflect payload around it.\n- Isolated red pixel (alone, no payload) → point-reflect each adjacent 8-connected color component.\n- Originals remain; mirrored pixels overlay.\n\nKey insight: Red marker geometry (line vs single pixel) determines reflection type; isolated vs embedded red determines what gets reflected.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:2978:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:8602:        "src": "colored sprites s + red marker pixels",
