/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3026:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:11633:        "src": "marker pixel set s with different colored center pixel and peripheral pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3027:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:11646:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3028:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:11690:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3029:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:11927:      "docstring": "Complete partial paths inside a framed rectangle by projecting external color traces inward.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg, a 1px rectangular frame (border color) with uniform interior fill.\n- Colored components outside the frame touching its edges.\n\nRule:\n- Output = the frame's interior, filled with the fill color.\n- Map each outside component's frame-touch points into interior coordinates.\n- Monochrome components become solid Manhattan stripes between mapped endpoints.\n- Two-color components become alternating-color Manhattan paths.\n\nKey insight: Endpoint colors of two-color traces anchor the alternating phase deterministically.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3030:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14374:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3031:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:15241:      "docstring": "Expand each colored control pixel into its corresponding fixed 4x4 glyph.\n\nInput structure:\n- Black background with single-pixel markers in colors 2, 3, 5, and/or 8.\n- Some inputs also show a sample 4x4 glyph in the output color, with a same-rule marker just below-right of the sample.\n\nRule:\n- Replace each marker color by its learned 4x4 glyph: 2->yellow frame, 3->blue ring, 5->pink diagonal blocks, 8->orange X.\n- Paint each glyph with its top-left corner at the marker pixel, clipping at the grid boundary.\n- Remove the sample glyphs and skip their below-right label markers.\n\nKey insight:\n- The colored pixels are control pixels for a fixed glyph alphabet; non-control sample glyphs are only legend entries, not preserved scene objects.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3032:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:15245:        "src": "single-pixel markers in the glyph alphabet colors",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3033:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:15246:        "transform": "replace each marker by its fixed 4x4 glyph, clipped at grid edge; sample glyphs and their below-right labels disappear"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3034:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:15256:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3035:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:15310:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3036:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:15311:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3037:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:15874:      "docstring": "Assemble scattered colored fragments into a left-right symmetric rectangle, jigsaw-style.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color; remaining colors form small sprite fragments.\n- Optional roles: 4 singleton pixels of one color mark corners; horizontal bars mark top/bottom edges; paired vertical lines mark left/right edges.\n\nRule:\n- Collect all non-bg connected components as jigsaw pieces.\n- Determine output rectangle dimensions from total piece area.\n- Pack pieces into the rectangle so it is exactly mirror-symmetric (left-right) and same-color pieces never 4-touch.\n\nKey insight: Left-right symmetry plus the no-same-color-touching constraint make the assembly unique; corner/edge markers anchor it when present.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3038:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:15912:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3039:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:15988:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3040:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:16107:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3041:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:16858:      "docstring": "Repair a one-cell-thick colored line network by replacing singleton markers, filling short orthogonal gaps, and redirecting yellow-marked arms to the edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- A rectangular grid with a dominant background.\n- Line colors form one-cell-thick horizontal/vertical stroke fragments.\n- Marker colors are exactly those whose 4-connected components are all singleton pixels.\n- Red singleton markers are missing line cells; yellow singleton markers are directional controls next to a line endpoint.\n\nRule:\n- Assign every marker to the nearest visible line color in row/column line-of-sight, preferring an endpoint supported along that same axis.\n- For each line color, fill the gap between consecutive facing endpoints in a row or column.\n- A yellow control erases the old straight arm on the far side of its endpoint and paints the same color from that endpoint through the control pixel to the grid edge.\n- At crossings, yellow-control rays win; otherwise an original-vs-filled crossing uses the more fragmented pre-repair line color, while pure filled crossings use the lower color id.\n\nKey insight: The singleton markers identify which sparse stroke fragments belong together; after they are colored, the intended lines are the axis-aligned gaps between facing endpoints, with yellow controls flipping one arm to the marked side.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3042:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:16862:        "src": "one-cell-thick colored line network with singleton red/yellow marker pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3043:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:16863:        "transform": "replace each marker by its assigned line color, fill facing horizontal/vertical gaps, and use yellow controls to erase the old arm and paint the same color from the endpoint through the marker to the grid edge",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3044:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:16864:        "notes": "crossings prefer yellow-control rays; otherwise original-vs-filled crossings use the more fragmented repaired line, and marker-bracketed filled gaps beat unmarked pure fills"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3045:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:16870:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3046:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:16878:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3047:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:16963:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3048:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:16964:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3049:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17044:      "docstring": "Align a central rectangle to two colored frame-edge controls via rotation/reflection.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg grid with two solid-colored border edges (distinct non-bg colors).\n- A central filled rectangle with 1px colored guide edges on two sides, colors matching the frame controls.\n\nRule:\n- Rotate/mirror the object so its guide edges face the same sides as the matching frame controls.\n- Crop off the 1px guide edges from aligned sides.\n\nKey insight: Guide-edge colors encode target frame sides; the correct dihedral transform matches both simultaneously.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3050:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17431:      "docstring": "Extend each colored marker from its directional sprite to a grid edge, painting a dotted ray and the whole edge side.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- One repeated body color forms small 8-connected directional sprites.\n- Each marker is a singleton non-background, non-body color embedded in one sprite.\n\nRule:\n- The body pixels around a marker lie mostly behind it; the opposite direction is the marker's ray direction.\n- Paint every second pixel from the marker along that ray, then paint the entire boundary side reached by the ray.\n- If two painted boundary sides meet at a corner, make that shared corner black.\n\nKey insight:\n- The same seven-pixel body sprite rotates to encode the direction; its local center-of-mass bias points away from the ray.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3051:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17435:        "src": "singleton colored markers embedded in seven-pixel directional body-color sprites",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3052:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17436:        "path": "cast from each marker in the direction opposite the sprite body bias to a grid boundary side",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3053:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17437:        "trajectory": "paint every second pixel along the ray, then paint the full reached boundary side in the marker color",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3054:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17450:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3055:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17508:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3056:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17509:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3057:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17569:      "docstring": "Paint the teal outline of the right triangle determined by the missing corner of the grey-marker square.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid is an orange background with exactly four foreground marker pixels of one color. The markers have a square bounding box: three markers are bbox corners, and the fourth marker is inside that square.\nRule\nFind the one corner of the marker bounding square that has no marker. That missing corner is the right-angle vertex of a right isosceles triangle; paint its two axis-aligned legs and the opposite diagonal in teal, leaving existing marker pixels unchanged.\nKey insight\nThe present corner marker opposite the missing corner is a decoy; the three triangle vertices are the missing corner and the two marker corners adjacent to it.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3058:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17573:        "src": "four grey marker pixels whose bbox is a square with exactly one missing corner",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3059:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17574:        "transform": "paint teal on the outline of the right triangle inside the square: the missing bbox corner is the right-angle vertex, the two adjacent marker corners are the other vertices; keep grey markers unchanged"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3060:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17578:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3061:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17583:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3062:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17633:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3063:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:17634:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3064:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18068:      "docstring": "Move each marker from a lattice corner gap into the adjacent enclosed 12-pixel cavity.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid is a repeated teal lattice around black 12-pixel cavities.\n- A marker is a non-black pixel placed at the northwest corner gap of one\n  complete 5x5 lattice tile; the marker may itself be teal.\n\nRule:\n- For every marked northwest corner gap, clear that marker to black.\n- Fill the 12 black pixels in the tile immediately down-right of the marker\n  with the marker color.\n- Leave the rest of the lattice unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- The apparent isolated markers are control pixels for the adjacent cavity;\n  teal markers are recognized as extra teal pixels occupying a gap that the\n  periodic lattice template says should be black.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3065:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18072:        "src": "non-black marker pixels at northwest corner gaps of 5x5 teal lattice tiles",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3066:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18073:        "transform": "erase each marker; fill the 12 black pixels in the adjacent down-right cavity with marker color",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3067:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18074:        "notes": "a teal marker is an extra teal pixel in a gap that the lattice template otherwise leaves black"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3068:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18080:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3069:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18087:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3070:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18140:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3071:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18141:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3072:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18188:      "docstring": "Use the pink control pixel to choose where the maroon pixel belongs inside the grey 3x3 region, and turn the control pixel maroon.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid contains one 3x3 region made from eight grey pixels and one maroon pixel.\n- There is exactly one pink control pixel outside that region.\n\nRule:\n- Restore the old maroon cell in the 3x3 region to grey.\n- Compare the pink pixel to the 3x3 region: above/same band/below selects top/middle/bottom, and left/same band/right selects left/middle/right.\n- Paint the selected cell maroon and recolor the pink control pixel maroon.\n\nKey insight:\n- The pink pixel acts as a relative-position marker for a 3x3 target inside the grey region.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3073:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18201:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3074:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18239:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3075:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18285:      "docstring": "Move each gray marker along its green path until it reaches the cell next to a black-green-black gate, erasing the path behind it.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Foreground components are made from a path color, a paired gate-end color, and single marker pixels.\n- A gate is a straight end-center-end motif whose center has the path color and whose two ends share the gate-end color.\n\nRule:\n- In every 4-connected foreground component with exactly one marker and one gate, erase the marker and all path-color pixels except the gate center.\n- Place the marker on the unique path-color pixel adjacent to the gate center but not between the two gate ends.\n- Components without both a marker and a gate stay unchanged.\n\nKey insight: The black-green-black motif marks the stopping gate; the gray marker consumes the connected green path until it rests on the path cell immediately beside that gate.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3076:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18289:        "src": "grey marker in a 4-connected green path component with one black-green-black gate",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3077:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18290:        "path": "continuous green path from the marker toward the gate",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3078:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18291:        "trajectory": "move the marker along the green path to dst",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3079:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18293:        "transform": "erase the old marker and traversed green path except the gate center; leave components without both marker and gate unchanged"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3080:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18298:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3081:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18304:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3082:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18363:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3083:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18553:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3084:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18652:      "docstring": "Copy each marked sprite to every standalone marker of the same color and erase the original sources.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Each source is an 8-connected component containing a monochrome sprite and one marker pixel of another color.\n- Other isolated marker pixels may be destinations; marker colors with no source sprite are distractors.\n\nRule:\n- Clear the grid to background.\n- For every source marker color, place the sprite at each other marker of that color using the source marker as the anchor.\n- Keep each destination marker pixel in place; do not keep source sprites, source markers, or distractor markers.\n\nKey insight:\n- A colored marker is not part of the sprite geometry; it is the anchor that says where same-colored copies of that sprite should be stamped.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3085:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18656:        "src": "8-connected marked object s containing one marker pixel and a monochrome sprite",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3086:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18657:        "dst": "standalone marker pixel d",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3087:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18658:        "match_cond": "s.marker.color == d.color",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3088:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18659:        "transform": "erase the input; stamp s.sprite at each d using the marker as anchor, keep d, and delete source markers plus distractor markers"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3089:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18665:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3090:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18672:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3091:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18720:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3092:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18721:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3093:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18917:      "docstring": "Decode the colored slot map inside the marked motif and rebuild the motif lattice with those colors.\n\nInput structure:\n- A blank background surrounds a rectangular lattice of identical motifs.\n- The motif rows and columns are separated by one background line.\n- One motif has colored marker pixels in its internal odd-row/odd-column slots.\n\nRule:\n- The motif size is 2R+1 by 2C+1, where R by C is the motif lattice size.\n- Read the marked motif's odd internal slots as the color map for the R by C output motifs.\n- Slots that still contain the repeated motif color map to that repeated motif color.\n- Rebuild the compact lattice on a canvas filled with the repeated motif color,\n  painting each motif mask with its decoded color.\n\nKey insight:\n- The holes and filled odd slots inside one motif are a miniature legend for recoloring the entire repeated motif lattice.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3094:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18930:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3095:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18939:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3096:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:18999:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3097:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19158:      "docstring": "Paint a recolored diagonal copy from each L triomino source object.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- The only foreground objects are 4-connected red and grey L triominoes,\n  each occupying three pixels of a 2x2 box.\n\nRule:\n- Grey L objects paint a yellow copy translated one diagonal step toward\n  their missing 2x2 corner.\n- Red L objects paint a green copy translated one diagonal step away from\n  their missing 2x2 corner.\n- Copies are clipped by the grid boundary; red-derived green copies are\n  painted after grey-derived yellow copies where the projections collide.\n\nKey insight:\n- The missing corner of each 2x2 L object identifies its diagonal axis, and\n  the source color determines which side of that axis receives the copy.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3098:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19172:        "catalog:projection",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3099:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19244:        "projections",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3100:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19281:      "docstring": "Swap paired marker pixels across the largest foreground-color barrier, placing them just outside the barrier segment.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- One foreground color is the unique most frequent non-background color; its pixels form the stationary barrier.\n- Other foreground pixels are single markers, sometimes paired on opposite sides of one contiguous barrier segment in the same row or column.\n\nRule:\n- Scan each row and column that crosses exactly one contiguous barrier segment.\n- If the line has exactly one marker on each side of that segment, erase both source markers and place each marker in the cell immediately beyond the opposite side of the segment.\n- Lines with markers on only one side are unchanged; the barrier remains unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- The marker pairing is local to a row or column, and the destination is defined by the nearest cells outside the intervening barrier segment, not by the original distance from the barrier.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3101:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19285:        "src": "single marker pixels that have exactly one marker on the opposite side of the same row or column through the largest foreground-color barrier",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3102:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19288:        "trajectory": "paint only the final adjacent cell on each side with the opposite marker color",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3103:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19289:        "transform": "erase the original paired marker cells; leave the barrier and unpaired markers unchanged"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3104:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19294:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3105:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19300:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3106:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19358:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3107:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19359:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3108:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19421:      "docstring": "Replace each marker below the separator with the mapped top legend square centered on that marker.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background surrounds a top legend, one solid non-background separator row, and a lower marker field.\n- The legend contains equal-size filled square sprites, with a singleton marker below each sprite and aligned to its center column.\n- The lower field contains only background and marker colors from the legend.\n\nRule:\n- Pair legend markers to legend sprites by left-to-right position.\n- Discard the legend and separator; keep the grid width and the rows below the separator.\n- In the lower field, replace every marker pixel by a filled square of the paired sprite color, centered at the marker location.\n\nKey insight: The top area is a positional color legend, and the actual output is the post-separator marker field expanded by that legend.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3109:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19426:        "dst": "lower marker d as center anchor",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3110:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19427:        "match_cond": "d.color == singleton marker color below s",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3111:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19428:        "symbol_instructions": "top legend maps each singleton marker color to its filled square sprite",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3112:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19440:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3113:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19492:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3114:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19493:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3115:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19815:      "docstring": "Mark the center of each odd-sized solid square with the plus marker color, erasing the marker only when it is outside the marked-center field.\n\nInput structure:\n- The dominant color is background.\n- Exactly two foreground colors are present: one unique 3x3 plus marker and one color forming separated solid square objects.\n\nRule:\n- For every non-marker 4-connected object, assert it is a solid square.\n- If the square side length is odd, recolor its center pixel to the plus marker color; even-sided squares stay unchanged.\n- Preserve the plus marker when its center lies inside the bounding box of the odd-square centers; otherwise erase it to background.\n\nKey insight:\n- Odd-sided solid squares have a single visible center pixel, and the plus supplies the color used to identify those centers.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3116:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19819:        "src": "a unique 4-connected 5-pixel plus marker and 4-connected solid square objects of the other foreground color",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3117:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19820:        "transform": "recolor the center pixel of each odd-sided solid square to the plus marker color; leave even-sided squares unchanged; erase the plus marker when its center is outside the bbox of the recolored centers"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3118:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19831:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3119:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19882:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3120:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19938:      "docstring": "Fold each straight red rod at its black marker, leaving the gray-anchored side fixed.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Each foreground object is a straight horizontal or vertical 4-connected rod.\n- Each rod contains many pixels of one line color, one endpoint marker, and one\n  interior control marker.\n\nRule:\n- For every rod, keep the segment from the endpoint marker through the control\n  marker unchanged.\n- Move the line-color tail on the far side of the control marker to a\n  perpendicular ray starting next to that marker.\n- Choose the perpendicular direction with more space to the grid edge.\n\nKey insight:\n- The endpoint marker identifies the fixed side of the rod, while the control\n  marker is the hinge; the tail folds into the larger open half-plane.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3121:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19945:        "transform": "clear the original tail; keep the markers and the gray-to-black segment fixed"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3122:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:19955:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3123:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:20015:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3124:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:20016:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3125:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:20299:      "docstring": "Merge same-sized filled rectangular objects by overlaying their internal marker pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background surrounds two or more separated 4-connected foreground objects.\n- Every object is a filled rectangle of the same size.\n- Each rectangle has the same majority base color plus one or more non-base marker pixels.\n\nRule:\n- Create one output rectangle with the shared object size, filled with the shared base color.\n- For each input rectangle, copy every non-base marker pixel to the same relative location\n  in the output.\n- Marker overlays must either land on base color or agree in color with an existing marker.\n\nKey insight:\nThe separated rectangles are layers of the same template; their colored marker pixels\ncombine by local coordinates while the repeated base fill is just the output canvas.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3126:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:20303:        "src": "non-base marker pixel s inside a same-sized filled rectangle",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3127:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:20311:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3128:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:20320:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3129:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:20374:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3130:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:20664:      "docstring": "Paint each pink control pixel as a teal horizontal bar whose reach equals the foreground counts on that row.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background color and one or more pink control pixels.\n- Each marker row has exactly one pink pixel; all other non-background pixels\n  in that row are counters.\nRule\n- Start from an all-background output grid.\n- For each pink pixel, count non-background pixels strictly to its left and\n  strictly to its right in the same row.\n- Paint teal from c - left_count through c + right_count on that row.\nKey insight\n- The foreground pixels are not copied; only their counts on each side of\n  each pink marker encode the teal bar length.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3131:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:20678:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3132:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:20724:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3133:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:21249:      "docstring": "Erase each target-color object crossed by the ray pointed by the bar-and-control marker.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- There is one three-pixel straight marker bar and one singleton control pixel adjacent to the bar center.\n- The remaining non-background color forms multiple 4-connected target objects.\n\nRule:\n- Cast a straight ray from the marker bar center in the direction away from the adjacent control pixel.\n- Find every 4-connected target-color object that intersects that ray.\n- Recolor all pixels of those hit target objects to the background; all other pixels stay unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- The whole object is erased when the center ray touches any of its pixels; the full marker bar width is not swept.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3134:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:21253:        "src": "three-pixel marker bar with an adjacent singleton control pixel",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3135:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:21256:        "transform": "recolor all pixels of selected target objects to background; leave the marker and other target objects unchanged"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3136:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:21270:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3137:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:21324:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3138:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:21379:      "docstring": "Remove each fracture marker line and push the surrounding object pixels one cell away from it.\n\nInput structure\n- A background grid with 8-connected foreground objects made from a body color and a rarer marker color.\n- Each object has a non-square bbox; the marker pixels form one complete fracture line across the shorter bbox axis.\n\nRule\n- Erase all marker pixels.\n- For a wide object, each row has one marker; body pixels left of it shift one cell left and body pixels right of it shift one cell right.\n- For a tall object, each column has one marker; body pixels above it shift one cell up and body pixels below it shift one cell down.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker line is a crack through the object, so the two sides separate by one pixel perpendicular to the crack.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3139:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:21383:        "src": "8-connected body-color objects on the background, each crossed by a rarer marker-color fracture line",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3140:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:21384:        "transform": "erase the marker pixels; in each wide object shift body pixels one cell left/right away from the row marker, and in each tall object shift body pixels one cell up/down away from the column marker"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3141:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:21389:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3142:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:21396:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3143:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:21443:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3144:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:21650:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3145:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:22022:      "docstring": "Fill every row from the nearest marked horizontal bar, turning bar rows and color-boundary ties into separator rows.\n\nInput structure\n- A dominant background fills the grid except for full-width horizontal bars and one vertical marker column.\n- Outside the marker column, every row is monochrome: either background or a source bar color.\n- Background rows share one marker color in the marker column; source bar rows share the other.\n\nRule\n- Each non-source row takes the color of the nearest source bar, with that row's marker-column pixel set to the source-marker color.\n- If a row is exactly midway between nearest bars of different colors, make the whole row the source-marker color.\n- Each original source bar row becomes a source-marker row with the marker-column pixel changed to the background-row marker color.\n\nKey insight\n- The marked bars are horizontal seeds for a one-dimensional nearest-seed partition over rows; equal-distance rows are separators only when the competing seed colors differ.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3146:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:22026:        "src": "marked horizontal bars and the vertical marker column",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3147:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:22027:        "transform": "recolor each row by the nearest source bar color; each source bar row becomes a marker separator row, and equal-distance rows between different bar colors become plain separator rows"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3148:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:22038:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3149:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:22090:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3150:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:22500:      "docstring": "Complete a four-corner framed rectangle from one decorated anchor rectangle and its diagonal mate.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Two same-color solid rectangular anchors of the same size sit on opposite\n  diagonal corners, with the first anchor above-left of the second.\n- The upper-left anchor has two one-cell-thick vertical control bars to its\n  right and two one-cell-thick horizontal control bars below it.\n\nRule:\n- Copy the anchor rectangle into the two missing corners of the implied\n  larger rectangle.\n- Repeat the right-side control bars horizontally between the left and right\n  anchors, using their spacing as the period, and draw the outer top and\n  bottom borders in the first right-control color.\n- Repeat the below-side control bars vertically between the top and bottom\n  anchors, using the same period, and draw the outer left and right borders\n  in the first below-control color.\n\nKey insight: The small control bars are the first two ticks of two periodic\nframe patterns; the diagonal anchor supplies the opposite corner and the\nmissing two anchor copies.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3151:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23204:        "src": "black 4-connected cutouts shaped as a solid rectangle plus a two-pixel tail, and multi-pixel colored source regions; a source color with a detached one-pixel marker is a decoy",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3152:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23215:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3153:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23268:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3154:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23449:      "docstring": "Infer the background, rotate the whole input 90 degrees counterclockwise, and stack two framed copies vertically.\n\nInput structure:\n- Blue is absent from the input.\n- One rare marker color appears in exactly two pixels.\n- The background is the unique non-marker color whose removal leaves exactly two 4-connected foreground objects, each with one marker pixel and one body color.\n- The whole grid, including background and foreground objects, is the sprite to transform.\n\nRule:\n- Rotate the entire input grid 90 degrees counterclockwise.\n- Create a blue one-pixel frame around two vertical copies of the rotated grid.\n- Use the input background color for the two endpoints of every horizontal frame/separator row.\n\nKey insight: The output is not a crop of the foreground objects; it is two copies of the complete rotated input, separated and enclosed by a newly added blue border.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3155:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23469:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3156:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23536:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3157:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23592:      "docstring": "Normalize vertical two-color bars between paired marker columns around the marker rows.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- A row of red marker pixels sits directly above a row of gray marker pixels\n  in the same alternating columns.\n- The columns between adjacent markers contain vertical bars made from a\n  contiguous teal run above a contiguous blue run.\n\nRule\n- Keep the marker pixels and all non-bar background cells fixed.\n- Let h be the maximum teal-run height among the bar columns; paint teal in\n  every bar column for h rows ending at the red marker row.\n- In each bar column, move its blue run to start at the gray marker row and\n  fill all lower cells in that column with maroon.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker rows are a baseline: teal is normalized into a common upper\n  band, while each blue run keeps its own height below the baseline.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3158:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23596:        "src": "vertical bar columns between paired red and gray marker columns; each bar is a teal run above a blue run",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3159:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23597:        "transform": "replace the bar columns with normalized bars: paint a full-width teal band of maximum teal-run height ending on the red marker row, move each blue run to start on the gray marker row, and fill lower cells in that column maroon"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3160:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23601:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3161:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23605:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3162:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23666:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3163:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23667:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3164:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23714:      "docstring": "Crop the foreground object whose missing cells match marker shapes, and fill those missing cells with the marker colors.\n\nInput structure\nA dominant background surrounds several monochromatic foreground objects. Exactly one object has background gaps inside its bounding box whose component shapes are matched by separate marker objects.\nRule\nFind that object, crop its bounding box, and replace each background gap component with the color of the separate marker component or components having the same normalized shape.\nKey insight\nThe marker objects do not mark absolute positions; their shapes identify which gaps in the selected object should be colored, while objects with unmatched gaps are distractors.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3165:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23718:        "src": "separate marker object s outside the selected object's bbox",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3166:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23736:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3167:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:23788:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3168:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:24437:      "docstring": "Advance the marker from one half of a vertical bar to the same half of the next longer bar.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has one dominant background color and exactly two foreground colors.\n- One foreground color forms many vertical one-cell-wide bars; the other appears as a single vertical marker segment.\n- The marker segment occupies exactly the top or bottom half of its containing vertical bar.\nRule\n- Recolor the current marker segment back to the bar color.\n- Find the unique all-bar-color vertical bar whose height is two pixels greater than the marked source bar.\n- Recolor the same half of that next longer bar to the marker color.\nKey insight\n- Each bar's total height encodes an ordered size, and the marker advances from a 2k bar to the corresponding 2(k+1) bar while preserving whether it marks the top or bottom half.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3169:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:24441:        "src": "a vertical marker segment occupying the top or bottom half of one bar, plus all-bar-color vertical bars of even heights",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3170:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:24442:        "transform": "erase the current marker to the bar color, then recolor the same half of the unique all-bar-color bar whose height is two pixels greater than the source bar"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3171:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:24454:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3172:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:24508:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3173:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25702:      "docstring": "Move each marked L-shaped sprite onto the separate pixel matching its marker color.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Foreground has 4-connected multicolor sprites and isolated one-pixel controls.\n- Each sprite has one repeated body color in an L shape plus one embedded marker\n  pixel of a different color.\n\nRule\n- If the embedded marker color also appears as a separate isolated control pixel,\n  translate the whole sprite so the body L-bend lands on that control pixel.\n- Clear each moved sprite from its old position, clear its consumed control pixel,\n  then paste all translated sprites; sprites without a matching control stay put.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker color pairs a sprite with its destination control, while the L-bend\n  gives the orientation-independent anchor cell to place on that destination.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3174:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25706:        "src": "marked L-shaped sprite s with one embedded marker pixel",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3175:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25708:        "match_cond": "s.marker.color == d.color and d lies on the outer diagonal ray from s.L_bend through s.marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3176:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25721:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3177:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25772:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3178:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25958:      "docstring": "Push every colored object touching maroon markers straight outward until it reaches the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Maroon pixels are fixed markers.\n- Every other foreground 4-connected object touches the marker pixels on exactly one cardinal side.\n\nRule:\n- Clear each non-background, non-maroon object from its original position.\n- Translate it in the direction away from its maroon contact until the object reaches the grid boundary.\n- Keep the maroon marker pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- The maroon contact side is a launcher: it determines a unique outward ray for the whole object, and the edge of the grid determines the translation distance.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3179:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25962:        "src": "non-background, non-maroon 4-connected objects touching maroon marker pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3180:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25966:        "transform": "clear each moving object from its original position; keep maroon markers unchanged"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3181:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25970:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3182:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:25977:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3183:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26029:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3184:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26030:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3185:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26318:      "docstring": "Extract the single plain rectangle and redraw it with the aligned rectangles' border-relative marker pattern.\n\nInput structure:\n- The boundary color is the background/separator.\n- Foreground objects are dense rectangular regions; exactly one rectangle has only its base color.\n- Other rectangles contain their base color plus marker pixels.\n\nRule:\n- Crop the only plain rectangle; this crop is the output canvas.\n- Use marked rectangles whose row span overlaps the plain rectangle's row span.\n- Transfer their marker pixels by preserving each marker run's distance from the nearest rectangle edges.\n\nKey insight:\n- The marked rectangles are examples of an edge-relative pattern, so the missing plain rectangle receives the same pattern resized to its own dimensions.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3186:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26322:        "src": "edge-relative marker run s in a marked rectangle aligned with the plain rectangle row band",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3187:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26325:        "transform": "paint each matched d with the shared marker color; keep base rectangle fill elsewhere",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3188:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26331:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3189:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26340:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3190:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26396:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3191:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26474:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3192:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26698:      "docstring": "Connect the innermost mirrored marker pair(s) by filling their horizontal span.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has one background color and one foreground color.\n- Each foreground row contains exactly two foreground pixels mirrored across the vertical center.\n\nRule\n- Find the foreground row pair(s) with the smallest horizontal gap between the two markers.\n- Fill every pixel between those two markers in each selected row with the foreground color.\n- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- Wider marker pairs are context; the closest marker pair(s) show the unresolved horizontal segment.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3193:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26702:        "src": "rows containing two horizontally mirrored foreground marker pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3194:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26703:        "transform": "find the row(s) whose marker pair has the smallest horizontal gap and fill the inclusive segment between those markers with the foreground color"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3195:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26707:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3196:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26712:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3197:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26755:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3198:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26756:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3199:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26798:      "docstring": "Use the left-edge color legend to draw a padded rectangular halo around each matching object while preserving enclosed holes.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a dominant background color.\n- One or more two-row markers sit on the left edge; each marker is a 2x2 block whose left column is an object color and right column is its halo color.\n- Away from the markers, every source color from the legend appears as one or more 4-connected monochrome objects.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the input pixels unchanged.\n- For each source-color object, take its tight bbox expanded by one cell and clipped to the grid.\n- Recolor background pixels in that expanded region to the marker's halo color, except for background holes enclosed by the object.\n\nKey insight:\n- The small left-edge bars are a legend: they map object colors to the colors used for the surrounding padded bbox.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3200:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26802:        "src": "4-connected monochrome objects on the background plus left-edge two-column color legend markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3201:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26818:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3202:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26876:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3203:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:26877:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3204:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27167:      "docstring": "Compact the checkerboard's moving color toward the edge marked by the teal pixel, leaving a maroon swept trail on the marker line.\n\nInput structure\n- A blue/black checkerboard with exactly one teal marker replacing a blue pixel on a non-corner edge.\n- The marker's checkerboard parity identifies the moving color (blue); the opposite parity is background (black).\n\nRule\n- If the marker is on the left or right edge, compact moving-color pixels in every row toward that side.\n- If the marker is on the top or bottom edge, compact moving-color pixels in every column toward that side.\n- Preserve the teal marker at its edge cell.\n- On the marker's row or column, color cells swept by shifted moving pixels maroon unless the final compacted line occupies them.\n\nKey insight\nThe marker selects both the compression direction and the checkerboard color class that moves; maroon records the movement trail only along that marked line.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3205:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27171:        "src": "moving-color pixels of the two-color checkerboard; the teal edge marker identifies the moving-color parity",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3206:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27172:        "path": "straight along each row toward a left/right marker edge, or along each column toward a top/bottom marker edge",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3207:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27173:        "trajectory": "stably compact all moving-color pixels to the marker edge in every parallel line",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3208:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27174:        "transform": "preserve the teal marker at its edge cell; on the marker row or column recolor swept vacated cells maroon unless occupied by the final compacted line"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3209:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27181:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3210:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27229:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3211:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27404:      "docstring": "Complete the sparse colored marker pattern by reflecting it across a full-row/full-column cross.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has a dominant background and one non-background cross color that\nfills exactly one complete row and one complete column. All other foreground\npixels are sparse markers away from that cross.\n\nRule\nKeep the input unchanged, and for each marker pixel copy its color to the\npositions obtained by reflecting it across the cross row, across the cross\ncolumn, and across both axes. Reflected positions outside the grid are\nclipped.\n\nKey insight\nThe full cross is not a copied object; it is the pair of mirror axes for\ncompleting the quadrant pattern.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3212:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27408:        "src": "sparse non-background marker pixels on one side of a full-row/full-column cross",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3213:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27410:        "transform": "copy each marker color to its horizontal, vertical, and double-reflection positions; clip reflected positions outside the grid; keep the cross and originals unchanged"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3214:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27414:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3215:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27419:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3216:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27467:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3217:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27468:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3218:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27804:      "docstring": "Recover each partially hidden 6x6 ring sprite and stack complete copies from top layer to bottom layer.\n\nInput structure:\n- The dominant color is the background.\n- Several non-background colors are visible fragments of the same 12-pixel\n  outline ring in a 6x6 box; small off-template marker pixels are noise.\n- Ring fragments overlap, so upper rings replace some expected pixels of\n  lower rings, and a ring may also be clipped by the input boundary.\n\nRule:\n- Identify every substantial color whose pixels all lie on one translated\n  copy of the ring template.\n- For each missing in-bounds template pixel, the color currently occupying\n  that pixel is above the hidden ring.\n- Topologically sort these occlusion relations from top to bottom, then draw\n  one complete 6x6 ring for each color in that order on a background canvas.\n\nKey insight:\n- The output is not a crop of the scene; it is the layer stack of complete\n  ring sprites reconstructed from their visible fragments.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3219:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27808:        "src": "visible fragments of overlapping 6x6 outline-ring sprites; sparse off-template colors are marker noise",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3220:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27817:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3221:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27822:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3222:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:27887:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3223:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28090:      "docstring": "Complete the sparse-color reflected copy of the foreground motif across its matching marker row or column.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has one background color and two foreground colors.\n- One foreground color appears only as a sparse marker row or column.\n- The other foreground color contains the same sparse marker positions on a parallel row or column, plus the motif on the far side of the sparse markers.\n\nRule\n- Keep the original grid unchanged.\n- Reflect every motif pixel of the larger foreground color across the two parallel marker lines.\n- Paint the reflected motif pixels with the sparse marker color.\n\nKey insight\n- The two equal marker rows or columns are paired landmarks: the sparse-color marker line borders the source motif, and the matching source-color marker line anchors the reflected copy.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3224:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28094:        "src": "larger foreground color: motif on one side of a sparse marker row or column, plus a matching marker line",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3225:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28095:        "dst": "background cells beyond the matching source-color marker line",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3226:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28096:        "transform": "reflect the motif across the pair of parallel marker lines and recolor it to the sparse marker color; keep all original pixels unchanged"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3227:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28104:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3228:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28148:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3229:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28149:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3230:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28215:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3231:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28445:      "docstring": "Project the framed periodic stripe pattern across the canvas and erase the unused frame cells.\n\nInput structure\n- A bg canvas with a one-cell-thick rectangular frame of one color.\n- Inside the frame are two parallel full-interior marker bars of another color.\n- A third color fills the region between the marker bars on periodically spaced rows or columns.\n\nRule\n- Infer the periodic row or column mask from the third-color stripes inside the frame.\n- Paint the frame color along those full rows or columns, extended to the grid boundary.\n- Extend the marker bars across the full canvas and repaint the source-color stripe cells between them.\n\nKey insight\n- The outer frame is not preserved as a border; it supplies the color for the periodic stripes selected by the inner source pattern.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3232:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28449:        "src": "one-color rectangular frame, two parallel full-interior marker bars, and periodic source-color stripes between the bars",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3233:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28450:        "dst": "same-size bg canvas with marker bars extended and the periodic stripe mask projected across the full grid",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3234:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28451:        "transform": "infer the source stripe period along the axis perpendicular to the marker bars; paint those whole rows or columns with the frame color, extend the marker bars across the canvas, and repaint source-color cells between the bars"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3235:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28463:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3236:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28513:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3237:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28699:      "docstring": "Drop every large foreground object straight down to the bottom while leaving small marker objects fixed.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a dominant background color and exactly one foreground color.\n- The foreground is split into separated 4-connected objects.\n- Objects of area at most three are stationary markers; larger objects are moving sprites.\n\nRule:\n- Clear each moving sprite from its original position.\n- Translate each moving sprite vertically downward until its bbox bottom reaches the grid bottom.\n- Repaint each translated sprite in its original color; small markers stay unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- Object area separates the active falling sprites from the small fixed markers, and all active sprites follow the same vertical path.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3238:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28715:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3239:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28769:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3240:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28770:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3241:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28834:      "docstring": "Rebuild the foreground rectangles as a largest-to-smallest lower-left nesting.\n\nInput structure\n- A periodic wallpaper background is overlaid by foreground colors that each form a rectangular frame or solid rectangle.\n- The largest foreground rectangle is the output frame; smaller foreground rectangles are the objects to nest inside it.\n- A frame may be partially hidden by a smaller rectangle, but its visible pixels still determine its bbox.\n\nRule\n- Ignore the wallpaper and crop the result to the largest foreground rectangle's bbox size.\n- Sort foreground rectangles by bbox area from largest to smallest.\n- Reconstruct each frame or solid rectangle, placing every next smaller rectangle in the lower-left of the current rectangle's usable region.\n\nKey insight\n- The scattered background colors are not objects; the meaningful order is the unique descending rectangle size chain, and each step nests into the previous rectangle's lower-left interior.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3242:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28840:        "transform": "discard the wallpaper; sort rectangles by bbox area descending; rebuild each frame or solid rectangle, placing each next smaller rectangle at the lower-left of the current frame interior or solid bbox",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3243:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28964:      "docstring": "Remove the left control column and roll the remaining image downward by the red marker's row.\n\nInput structure\n- The input is a rectangular grid with a one-cell-wide control column on the left.\n- That control column is all pink except for exactly one red marker pixel.\n- The columns to the right are the image that remains in the output.\n\nRule\n- Delete the left control column.\n- Let r be the row index of the red marker in that column.\n- Cyclically shift the remaining image downward by r rows.\n\nKey insight\n- The red marker's vertical position encodes the row-roll amount; the pink\n  column is only a control strip and is removed after reading it.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3244:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28968:        "src": "image rows to the right of a pink control column with one red marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3245:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28969:        "dst": "same-height output with rows cyclically ordered by the marker row",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3246:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28970:        "transform": "delete the control column; cyclically roll the remaining rows downward by the red marker's row index",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3247:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28971:        "symbol_instructions": "pink control column encodes a cyclic row shift; the red marker row gives the shift offset",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3248:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:28977:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3249:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29022:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3250:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29072:      "docstring": "Cast yellow horizontal and vertical rays from the teal rectangle until blue blockers stop them.\n\nInput structure:\n- A black-background grid containing one solid teal rectangle.\n- Blue objects are blockers; other non-background objects may lie in the ray paths.\n- Yellow is absent from the input and is the output paint color.\n\nRule:\n- From every row of the teal rectangle, cast rays left and right to the grid edge.\n- From every column of the teal rectangle, cast rays up and down to the grid edge.\n- A ray stops before a blue pixel; all crossed non-blue, non-teal pixels become yellow.\n\nKey insight:\nThe teal rectangle defines a full cross-shaped projection, while blue objects are walls and red/background cells are simply paintable space.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3251:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29083:        "catalog:projection",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3252:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29154:        "projection",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3253:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29320:      "docstring": "Advance short marker bars away from the full edge bar, turning completed two-pixel markers into edge-color marks at the opposite side.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- One non-background color forms a complete one-cell-thick bar on exactly one outer edge.\n- The other foreground color appears only in the first two cells inward from that bar, lane by lane.\n\nRule\n- In each lane perpendicular to the edge bar, a one-pixel marker adjacent to the bar grows one more cell inward.\n- A two-pixel marker in those first two inward cells is cleared back to background.\n- The cleared two-pixel marker is replaced by a two-pixel mark of the edge-bar color at the opposite side of the same lane.\n\nKey insight\n- The full edge bar defines both the orientation and the direction of the local two-step marker cycle.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3254:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29324:        "src": "one-pixel and two-pixel marker bars in lanes perpendicular to a complete edge bar",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3255:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29325:        "transform": "extend one-pixel markers one cell inward; clear two-pixel markers to bg and write a two-pixel edge-color mark at the opposite side of the same lane"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3256:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29334:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3257:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29386:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3258:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29387:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3259:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29430:      "docstring": "Recolor the row-wise passage indicated by wall pixels with the singleton marker color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background contains one singleton marker pixel and one wall color.\n- Wall pixels lie on several rows and form left/right limits around the marker column.\n- Empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows are open horizontal passages.\n\nRule:\n- On a wall row, paint background pixels between the nearest wall strictly\n  left of the marker column and the nearest wall at or right of it; if only\n  one side is present, paint from that wall to the opposite grid edge.\n- On empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows, paint the whole row.\n- On empty rows outside the wall-row band, reuse the nearest end wall-row interval.\n- Preserve wall pixels and the original marker pixel.\n\nKey insight:\n- The wall color defines scanline limits relative to the marker column; the\n  marker color fills those implied horizontal spans rather than flood-filling\n  through connected background.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3260:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29434:        "src": "one singleton marker pixel and rows of wall-color pixels on a dominant background",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3261:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29435:        "transform": "recolor background pixels in the scanline passage selected by the marker column: wall rows fill between nearest wall limits, empty interior rows fill full width, and empty exterior rows reuse the nearest end interval"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3262:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29445:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3263:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29500:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3264:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29561:      "docstring": "Crop off the control row and column, then cyclically roll the payload by the two marker offsets.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid is square, with a control row on top and a control column on the left.\n- The control row and column share one filler color and one single-pixel marker color.\n- The lower-right square is the payload and contains none of the control colors.\n\nRule\n- Remove the top control row and left control column.\n- Roll the remaining payload down by the marker's zero-based position in the left control column.\n- Roll the payload right by the marker's zero-based position in the top control row.\n\nKey insight\n- The two border markers are cyclic shift amounts for the payload, not colors to preserve.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3265:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29566:        "dst": "payload square with cyclic origin shifted by the control markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3266:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29567:        "transform": "crop off the control row/column; roll the payload down by the left marker offset and right by the top marker offset",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3267:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29578:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3268:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29621:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3269:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29622:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3270:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:29955:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3271:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30078:      "docstring": "Compress the L-shaped cue to three rows and add a pink copy of the top-row foreground mask.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has a dominant background color, a two-color top row, and all\nforeground pixels below the top row lie in the first column as vertical markers.\n\nRule\nKeep the input top row as output row 0 and the first marker row as output row 1.\nOutput row 2 is background except at the top-row foreground columns, which are\nrecolored pink.\n\nKey insight\nThe lower repeated marker rows only identify the vertical cue; the generated\nrow is a recolored mask of the horizontal cue in the top row.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3272:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30082:        "src": "L-shaped cue with a two-color top row and vertical marker pixels in the first column",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3273:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30084:        "transform": "keep the top row and first marker row; discard lower marker rows; make the third row background except for pink pixels at the top-row foreground columns",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3274:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30089:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3275:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30093:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3276:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30139:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3277:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30140:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3278:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30180:      "docstring": "Draw the marker-colored route through the centers of all doors in the parallel wall maze.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a background, parallel full-span walls, one three-pixel door\n  segment in each wall, and two marker pixels sharing a color.\n- Walls are either all vertical or all horizontal, and the markers are on\n  opposite outer sides of the wall set.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the scene unchanged except for the route.\n- Visit the door centers in wall order from the upper/left marker side to\n  the lower/right marker side.\n- In each corridor, draw an orthogonal path to the cell just before the next\n  wall, move along that wall to the door center, cross the center, and\n  continue to the next corridor; after the last door, connect to the other\n  marker.\n\nKey insight:\n- The three-pixel door segments mark the only crossing points through a set\n  of parallel walls, so the output is the corridor path threaded through\n  those centers.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3279:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30184:        "src": "two same-color marker pixels outside parallel walls with three-pixel door segments",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3280:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30185:        "path": "connect the markers through the center of each door in wall order, using orthogonal corridor segments just before crossing each wall",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3281:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30186:        "trajectory": "paint the continuous route with the marker color, including each door center",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3282:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30191:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3283:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30198:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3284:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30252:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3285:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30253:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3286:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30325:      "docstring": "Draw a blue folded corner-to-corner route through the lone marker's column.\n\nInput structure:\n- A rectangular grid filled with one background color.\n- Exactly one non-background marker pixel; blue is absent from the input.\n\nRule:\n- Preserve the marker and repaint background pixels in its column blue from top to bottom.\n- If the marker is in the unique center column, connect that column to the top-right and bottom-left corners.\n- Otherwise, connect the column to the top-left and bottom-right corners.\n\nKey insight:\nThe marker's column is the route spine; its central vs off-center placement selects which opposite corner pair gets the horizontal edge segments.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3287:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30329:        "src": "single non-background marker pixel in an otherwise solid background grid",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3288:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30330:        "path": "vertical route through the marker's column, plus horizontal edge segments to an opposite corner pair",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3289:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30332:        "dst": "connect to top-right and bottom-left corners if the marker is in the unique center column; otherwise connect to top-left and bottom-right corners",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3290:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30333:        "transform": "preserve the marker color and leave all non-route background pixels unchanged"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3291:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30341:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3292:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30386:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3293:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30928:      "docstring": "Crop the largest object and overlay each smaller sprite where its shared marker pattern matches.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the most common color, and the foreground has one largest destination object plus smaller source sprites.\n- Each source sprite shares exactly one marker color with the destination object.\n\nRule\n- Output the tight bbox crop of the largest object.\n- Translate each source sprite so every connected marker component of the shared color exactly matches destination marker components.\n- Paste source sprites in decreasing area order, so smaller sprites can sit on top of larger ones when they overlap.\n\nKey insight\n- The shared-color marker components are alignment keys; matching whole marker components distinguishes singleton slots from larger same-color marker blocks.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3294:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30932:        "src": "smaller 4-connected source sprite s with marker pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3295:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30933:        "dst": "marker component pattern d inside the largest destination object",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3296:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30934:        "match_cond": "s.marker components have the same shape and relative arrangement as d",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3297:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30942:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3298:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:30950:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3299:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31004:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3300:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31066:      "docstring": "Rotate each blue-started chain of bottom-aligned vertical bars into horizontal bars resting on the same baseline.\nInput structure\n- The grid has a background and bottom-aligned, one-cell-wide vertical bars.\n- Blue bars are markers; red bars are body bars that may be chained after a marker.\nRule\n- Starting at each blue bar, repeatedly include the next red bar whose column is exactly the current bar's column plus the current bar's height.\n- Clear every included vertical bar, then redraw each included bar horizontally to the right from its original bottom cell, with length equal to its vertical height.\n- Red bars that are not reached from a blue marker remain unchanged.\nKey insight\n- A vertical bar's height is also the width it occupies after rotation, so the chain follows immediate horizontal contact after each rotated bar.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3301:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31082:        "object:marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3302:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31139:        "marker",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3303:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31140:        "markers",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3304:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31443:      "docstring": "Replace the scattered foreground markers with a bottom-left count rectangle whose two corner diagonals encode the marker counts.\n\nInput structure\n- A background grid with exactly two foreground colors used as scattered marker pixels.\n- The two foreground colors have distinct pixel counts.\n\nRule\n- Ignore marker positions and use only the two foreground counts.\n- Make a 16-by-16 background canvas, fill a bottom-left red rectangle whose height is the smaller count and width is the larger count.\n- Paint yellow pixels along the two rising 45-degree diagonals from the rectangle's bottom-left and bottom-right corners.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker colors and positions vary between examples; their counts alone determine the output rectangle dimensions.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3305:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31447:        "src": "two foreground marker colors on the background; only their pixel counts matter",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3306:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31449:        "transform": "fill the rectangle red with height equal to the smaller marker count and width equal to the larger marker count; recolor the two rising diagonals from the bottom corners yellow",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/2/015/codegen_5.skill_011_020.log:3307:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:31454:        "catalog:marker_pixels",
